-- title:
--   Compact kernel average preserves slab profiles and Paley–Wiener form
-- statement:
--   Let $K$ be a number field, let $0<\alpha<\beta$ be reals, and let $\xi_K$ be a homomorphism from the full subgroup $\top$ of the idele units $(\mathbb{A}_K)^\times$ to $\mathbb{C}^\times$ which is continuous, trivial on the image of $K^\times$, and of absolute value $1$ everywhere; an ideal $N$ of $\mathcal{O}_K$ and an archimedean type family are carried along as parameters. Write $\alpha_m$ for the $\mathbb{R}^\times$-valued character obtained from the module character `distribHaarChar` of the adele ring, assumed everywhere positive. Given a continuous kernel $\kappa$ on the maximal compact subgroup `adelicMaximalCompact K` (matrices integral at all finite places and row-isometric at all infinite places) and an operator $P$ with $P\varphi(g)=\int \kappa(k)\varphi(gk)\,dk$ against the Haar measure of that subgroup; a finite index set $\iota_P$ with families of characters $\mu_e,\nu_e$ that are unitary, trivial on $K^\times$, continuous, satisfy $\mu_e\nu_e=\xi_K$, are permuted by an involution $r_P$ interchanging $\mu$ and $\nu$, and are pairwise separated on the norm-one ideles; and a family $\psi_e(s)$ of functions on $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{A}_K)$ which are induced sections for the Borel characters $\mu_e\,\alpha_m^{s+1/2}$ and $\nu_e\,\alpha_m^{-(s+1/2)}$, jointly continuous, holomorphic in $s$, archimedean $K$-finite, smooth for the finite-adelic subgroup, with $K$-types at each infinite place in a fixed finite-dimensional space, and dominated in vertical strips by a bounded integrable function after multiplication by $(1+|t|)^n$, uniformly on compacta. Suppose $\psi$ is a slab profile for the central subgroup of the production pins attached to $(\alpha,\beta)$, the principal levels intersected with the finite-adelic subgroup, the Hecke generators and the adelic box — that subgroup being $\top$ — and the character $\xi_K$: that is, $\psi$ is measurable, invariant under left translation by unipotent matrices and by global Borel points, satisfies $\psi(z g)=\xi_K(z)\psi(g)$ for central scalars, is bounded on each slab $\|\det g\|\in[d_1,d_2]$ with $d_1>0$, and vanishes outside a band $a\le \mathrm{ht}(g)\le b$ with $a>0$; and suppose $\psi(g)=\sum_e (4\pi)^{-1}\int_{\mathbb{R}}\psi_e(\sigma'+it)(g)\,dt$ for every real $\sigma'$ and every $g$. Then $P\psi$ is again such a slab profile with the same character $\xi_K$, and $P\psi(g)=\sum_e (4\pi)^{-1}\int_{\mathbb{R}} P(\psi_e(\sigma'+it))(g)\,dt$ for every real $\sigma'$ and every $g$.
--
--   This records that right convolution by a continuous kernel on the maximal compact subgroup preserves the class of slab profiles with a fixed central character and commutes with a Paley–Wiener integral representation by sections of induced representations; the slab conditions are either left-sided or invariant under right translation by the maximal compact, whose elements have idele-norm-one determinant and preserve the adelic height. It is used in the construction of pseudo-Eisenstein averages and the residual projection for kernels supported on the maximal compact.
